      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BEEJAY BOY (3) earns top billing after finishing seventh in stronger NMW1Y company at Ascot, beaten just under three lengths after having difficulty getting clear near the 150m. He is eased back from Saturday company, is now fourth-up, and his one win and two placings from six previous starts around 1720m puts him on top. SAUCISSON (5) comes through a different line after being beaten a head at York in BM44+ grade and gets meaningful weight relief, though he does rise in class from that near miss. SNIP OF GOSSIP (4) has the proven local angle, with a win and a placing from three starts at this track and distance, and his narrow Ascot second two runs back reads well for this. MISS WALL STREET (8) backs up quickly from a fair seventh in stronger NMW1Y company and gets a 3kg claim, but the step to 1720m still asks her to find a sharper finish.",
